Check program binaries before ANGLE deserializes them: a CRC and the size over every binary, on Metal and Vulkan.

Why: glProgramBinary handed ANGLE's deserializer the bytes as they came. A binary cut short or damaged, as a game
engine's shader cache can hold one after an update or a write that did not finish, made a count out of the bytes and
aborted the process in std::vector (length_error under -fno-exceptions), where Android's drivers refuse the binary
with a link status of false and the engine links from its source again. ANGLE's frontend feature
compressProgramBinaryBlob (upstream on for Samsung's Vulkan devices only) writes a header with a magic value, the
CRC32 and the size of the payload, and loadBinary refuses a binary whose header, size or CRC does not match before it
deserializes anything. The binaries get smaller too (zlib).
Test: fixtures program-binary-test (two starts: saved binaries loaded in a new process, then a binary of a format not
listed, one cut short, one with its middle overwritten, an empty one and one with bytes after its end).
Upstream: could go upstream (the deserializer's counts are the real fix).
Remove: when upstream checks every count it reads, or turns the feature on by default.

--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/DisplayMtl.mm
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/DisplayMtl.mm
@@ -516,6 +516,10 @@
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(features, linkJobIsThreadSafe, true);
 
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(features, setNeedInitOnInvalidation, true);
+
+    // Minato: program binaries carry a CRC and their size, so that a binary cut short or damaged is refused
+    // (link status false) before it is deserialized, as Android's drivers refuse one.
+    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(features, compressProgramBinaryBlob, true);
 }
 
 void DisplayMtl::populateFeatureList(angle::FeatureList *features)
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
@@ -7337,7 +7337,8 @@
 
     // Enable the program binary blob compression for glGetProgramBinary and glGetProgramiv.  It
     // will be decompressed when loading the program binary by glProgramBinary.
-    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(features, compressProgramBinaryBlob, isSamsung);
+    // Minato: on every device, so that a binary cut short or damaged is refused before it is deserialized.
+    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(features, compressProgramBinaryBlob, isSamsung || true);
 }
 
 angle::Result Renderer::getLockedPipelineCacheDataIfNew(vk::ErrorContext *context,
